"No, no my dear, they had if all wrong," said the woman who's wrinkles told the story of every life she had ever lived. "Its hard to get it right, that's sure, but they just.. well they got it all terrible wrong."

She served tea made from herbs she picked from small jars, each a unique tiny and she smelled each with the.consideration of a surgeon working on the nerves at the base of the spine. Assuring that each was just right, squinting eyes and licking lips. A perfect brew, a healing elixir, a meeting with a mystery person who's number you go through a series of seemingly benign and yet entirely connected experiences. And now you sit here, as she prepares for you a tea made of mysterious leaves of purple and yellow, the kind that is like golden red and not neon and unbearable. She seeps the leaves directly in the water, hot from a tea kettle made of black and golden, etched with intricately designed patterns of triangles and diamonds and lines crossing over lines. It reminded you of the ancient Egyptians and yet the attributes mirrored many other aritechrure and patterns found through many civilizations. The steam rose above the water, waves of patterned particles steaming upwards, laced with the tea, laced with the water, laced with the air and all bound together in a delicate dance drive to rise above the earth. A pure act of defiance against the laws we call gravity. Its own creature, free to act of it's own laws as long as they break no others.

"Alright darling, drink up," she hummed, pushing forward the hot cup and saucer. The same patterns adorned the beautiful materials and you wondered as the smell hit your nose, how you knew instantly they were in a language and the language said WE ARE ONE.

You see the problem is that any time we get to a place where the answer is not yet stated and the question itself may not have been asked that everyone balks and claims its hogwash and magic and entirely a lie. The earth is not the center of the solar system? Insanity. The world is made of all bow thing? Insanity. But eventually we come to agree and approve these new truths because there is no way to escape them. But at the beginning is always doubt. There is always the look of assumptions of insanity. there is always these ghastly people who are sure that we are the smartest of all creation because we are the creations we can see. But hundreds of years ago we could not see. We could.not know. We founded ideas as they came into us and we found them right but it was always first an idea.